# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'pallet-asset-conversion: support per-pair swap fee (fallback to global LPFee)'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      `pallet-asset-conversion` now supports an optional per-pool swap fee that overrides the
      global `Config::LPFee`. The change is additive and requires no storage migration: a new
      `PoolFees` storage map holds per-pool overrides, and when a pool has no entry the global
      `LPFee` continues to apply. Existing pools and runtimes are unaffected.

      New items:
      - `Config::AdminOrigin`: the origin permitted to change a pool's fee after creation.
      - `PoolFees` storage map (`PoolId -> Permill`).
      - `create_pool_with_fee` extrinsic: like `create_pool`, but lets the creator set an initial
        per-pool fee. `create_pool` is unchanged.
      - `set_pool_fee` extrinsic: sets the fee of an existing pool, gated by `AdminOrigin`.
      - `PoolFeeSet` event.
      - `Pallet::pool_fee` / `get_amount_out_with_fee` / `get_amount_in_with_fee` helpers. The
        existing `get_amount_out` / `get_amount_in` keep their signatures and use the global
        `LPFee`.

      Integration: runtimes implementing `pallet_asset_conversion::Config` must now provide an
      `AdminOrigin` (e.g. `EnsureRoot`).

  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |-
      Liquidity pools on asset-conversion can now charge a swap fee that differs from the global
      default, set at pool creation via `create_pool_with_fee` or afterwards by governance via
      `set_pool_fee`. Pools without an explicit fee behave exactly as before.

crates:
  - name: pallet-asset-conversion
    bump: major
  - name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: kitchensink-runtime
    bump: minor
